{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367413-what-makes-a-bloodline-a-bloodline","id":1367413,"title":"What makes a Bloodline a Bloodline?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-13T00:38:55-08:00","id":1367413,"title":"What makes a Bloodline a Bloodline?","content":"I recently got my hands on a copy of the new Spilled Blood book, as well as copies of Bloodlines: The Resurrected and The Devoted. I always thought Bloodlines were meant to be small groups of Kindred who possessed a special quirk to their Vitae that gave them access to unique powers, typically in the form of Disciplines and Devotions available only to members of the particular Bloodline, but I'm seeing a lot of Bloodlines in the three books that don't match this description. In fact they tend to be little more than small groups of Kindred that share nothing more than an ideology. Take the Ankou for example. What makes them a Bloodline? They're basically just a group of vampires who wish to maintain the balance between humans and vampires. There isn't really anything that makes them stand out from their parent clan. If a shared ideology is enough to make a Bloodline then why aren't the Brood a Bloodline. They're basically the same thing. The brood even get some unique toys to play with while the Ankou get nothing. In Resurrected and Devoted there are a handful of Bloodlines that are basically all just different kinds of vampire necromancers. Isn't that like saying the Lancea or Circle should just be a collection of Bloodlines that all have access to their forms of blood magic? Am I missing something? Are Bloodlines not what I'm thinking they are? Are the people who are writing these Bloodlines getting them confused with Mystery Cults or something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T03:55:22-08:00","id":1367479,"title":"","content":"Bloodlines have never been a singular concept. They apply to certain dynasties of Kindred, groupings based around ideologies and philosophies, and anything in-between. If you look at the 1e Covenant books you'll indeed see that each Covenant does contain multiple bloodlines almost exclusively found within that specific Covenant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T07:19:49-08:00","id":1367529,"title":"","content":"I think the idea is that bloodlines could be any of those things and you as a storyteller can choose what interpretation is appropriate for your chronicle. At the base level a bloodline is a vampire who has refined his blood to confer *some* special advantage or disadvantage, so by that token, the Ankou qualify with their added Vigor discipline, which is all they really need to do their job.<br /> <br /> It feels like the clans or bloodlines were written explicitly to be easy convertible from one type to the other. Like, very little is stopping you from making the Amari or Nhand a bloodline instead of a clan, or demoting the Ankou to just a wing of the Invictus. It feels like a toolkit showcase rather than supplemental canon, which I rather like.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T12:54:27-08:00","id":1367584,"title":"","content":"Bloodlines can have their own little cultures; they've always had a bit of a cultish quality. Remember that, aside from Kindred who are brought into a bloodline by their sires after the Embrace, most vampires join their bloodlines later in their Requiems. You choose to change your blood if you believe in the cause enough. The clans are large enough that you can't really say &quot;Oh, the Mekhet are a Carthian clan&quot;, but bloodlines are by their nature fairly small, and are often focused around their founders' and their political machinations. If grandsire says be in the Invictus, you better damn well be in the Invictus.<br /> <br /> From an out of character perspective, bloodlines are kind of the way Requiem does sub-factions of both clans <i>and </i>covenants (though there are covenant groups that aren't bloodlines). It's a little less elegant than some of the other games and their &quot;z-splats&quot;, but vampires are also more tied by blood relationships than the other monsters; politics, religion, and family always end up in the mix.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, as much as I appreciate how much people enjoy Bloodlines: The Devoted and Resurrected, they're basically glorified homebrew. We put a lot of work into them, and they definitely fit into <i>my </i>aesthetic as a Requiem fan/writer, but they don't necessarily reflect how bloodlines work in official supplements (although we certainly try not to take them too far from the baseline).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 02-13-2020, 03:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T13:08:11-08:00","id":1367587,"title":"","content":"And, unfortunately, leads to membership in a bloodline-based family being mutually exclusive with membership in bloodline-based ideological groups. Hell, even being of the wrong Clan makes it impossible to join such ideological groups even if you'd otherwise be a 100% match. Seems almost like a holdover from Masquerade where the Clans themselves were major factions.<br /> <br /> It's a shame Spilled Blood doesn't seem to have tidied up the bloodline concept for second edition. It's messy, but not the good kind of messy that propels interesting stories and mysteries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T13:34:23-08:00","id":1367594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367413-what-makes-a-bloodline-a-bloodline?p=1367587#post1367587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, unfortunately, leads to membership in a bloodline-based family being mutually exclusive with membership in bloodline-based ideological groups. Hell, even being of the wrong Clan makes it impossible to join such ideological groups even if you'd otherwise be a 100% match. Seems almost like a holdover from Masquerade where the Clans themselves were major factions.<br /> <br /> It's a shame Spilled Blood doesn't seem to have tidied up the bloodline concept for second edition. It's messy, but not the good kind of messy that propels interesting stories and mysteries.</div> </div> </div> </div>well for all the Mutations the Blood can accomplish, ultimately sometimes a specialized strain will be tied to a key clan. besides, you can still have them as allies if you cant join the bloodline<br /> <br /> vampire has always a theme of insular family, with childer and sire, and naturally, bloodlines. it adds to that idea, that the blood that connects you to similar beings does so because vampires see them as something to relate to","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T08:54:48-08:00","id":1367781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367413-what-makes-a-bloodline-a-bloodline#post1367413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recently got my hands on a copy of the new Spilled Blood book, as well as copies of Bloodlines: The Resurrected and The Devoted. I always thought Bloodlines were meant to be small groups of Kindred who possessed a special quirk to their Vitae that gave them access to unique powers, typically in the form of Disciplines and Devotions available only to members of the particular Bloodline, but I'm seeing a lot of Bloodlines in the three books that don't match this description. In fact they tend to be little more than small groups of Kindred that share nothing more than an ideology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh good. Nice to hear that not all bloodlines are using use the same tired formula. The tired formula was that bloodlines always got an affinity with a 4th discipline (often a unique discipline just to make them special), and another weakness.<br /> <br /> I was annoyed in 1E that many bloodlines had a unique bloodline disciplines that no one outside the bloodline could learn. It basically denied vampires from ever developing new or similar powers, not that developing new disciplines was a topic covered in any of the rules (from what I can recall).<br /> <br /> I look forward to reading those books (I've been away for a few years).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","name":"DivineWrath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T11:47:37-08:00","id":1367822,"title":"","content":"The sample Bloodlines that came out pretty soon after Second Edition already played with that standard. They all get four Disciplines, as the core book defines all Bloodlines as getting a fourth Discipline, but their Bloodline Gifts are not Unique Disciplines.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-jaws-of-the-beast/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/the-jaws-of-the-beast/</a> Their Bloodline Gift is a series of unique Merits, rather than a unique Discipline.<br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-shadow-and-the-asp/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/the-shadow-and-the-asp/</a> is a series of unique Devotions, not a Discipline<br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/lonely-together/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/lonely-together/</a> is simply passive abilities<br /> <br /> It is my understanding that the design philosophy of 2e Bloodlines was meant to explicitly cut down on that glut of Unique Disciplines that nobody else can learn and clogs up design space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T12:28:01-08:00","id":1367832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367413-what-makes-a-bloodline-a-bloodline?p=1367822#post1367822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sample Bloodlines that came out pretty soon after Second Edition already played with that standard. They all get four Disciplines, as the core book defines all Bloodlines as getting a fourth Discipline, but their Bloodline Gifts are not Unique Disciplines.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-jaws-of-the-beast/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/the-jaws-of-the-beast/</a> Their Bloodline Gift is a series of unique Merits, rather than a unique Discipline.<br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-shadow-and-the-asp/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/the-shadow-and-the-asp/</a> is a series of unique Devotions, not a Discipline<br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/lonely-together/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/lonely-together/</a> is simply passive abilities<br /> <br /> It is my understanding that the design philosophy of 2e Bloodlines was meant to explicitly cut down on that glut of Unique Disciplines that nobody else can learn and clogs up design space.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are conceptual bloodlines from writers playing around, and not indicative of anything (especially considering that they were written before VtR lost/changed lead dev). The actually published bloodlines we do have (before Spilled Blood) both had a fourth unique Discipline. Cachexy for Morbus and Crochan for Bron. They follow the 1e format extremely closely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T13:23:22-08:00","id":1367847,"title":"","content":"I don't mind the covenant-style bloodlines or the ones without specific enumerated powers. My conception of a bloodline is that a Vampire (at high enough BP) made a change to their blood for a <i>purpose</i>, and that their bloodline should thematically embody that purpose through their bane, favored attributes, and Disciplines/Merits/Devotions. Ankou seem perfectly appropriate by that definition. Not all Vampires are going to go out of their way to craft super unique special powers. VtR isn't Mage <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Like with the Parliamentarians, could I imagine a Carthian so absolutely committed and dedicated to his obsessive pestering and argumentation that he took that change to his blood? I sure could. I like that the document specifies that even though they're exclusively created as part of the Carthian movement, the other covenants try to recruit them out of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367413-what-makes-a-bloodline-a-bloodline?p=1367587#post1367587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a shame Spilled Blood doesn't seem to have tidied up the bloodline concept for second edition. It's messy, but not the good kind of messy that propels interesting stories and mysteries.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'm like you in that I don't want the majority of bloodlines to be tied to covenants so strongly for exactly the reasons you mentioned. It would be my preference for writers to focus on bloodlines that are more accessible to more players/characters. At the same time, I like that this is an option as it reflects my understanding of what a Bloodline is supposed to be: someone had a specific goal and tried to shape their Blood to yield to it, and sometimes those goals can be fiercely political in nature.<br /> <br /> And if anything, gating a power through a Covenant actually still keeps the possibility for spill-out. Gating a power through a Clan actually makes it virtually inaccessible to 4/5 of all Vampires (.. or 19/20 if you're counting all the rare Clans :P).<br /> <br /> Tangent: if I'm counting correctly, out of some ~105 statted bloodlines from 1e, 45 don't have a unique Discipline, and about 60 do. So while unique Disciplines are a big part of Bloodlines, they obviously weren't the defining thematically important piece.<br /> <br /> I'm enjoying reading your thoughts about this, Tessie. Am I understanding your preference correctly that you hoped every Bloodline (or almost every) would come with a unique fourth Discipline or be locked only to a single clan?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T14:54:02-08:00","id":1367873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367413-what-makes-a-bloodline-a-bloodline?p=1367832#post1367832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those are conceptual bloodlines from writers playing around, and not indicative of anything (especially considering that they were written before VtR lost/changed lead dev).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Seems an odd position to take. They're as official as anything else. Especially given they are listed in the <i>Official </i>Resources post by Rose and posted on the official website/blog.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T14:56:12-08:00","id":1367877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367413-what-makes-a-bloodline-a-bloodline?p=1367847#post1367847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm enjoying reading your thoughts about this, Tessie. Am I understanding your preference correctly that you hoped every Bloodline (or almost every) would come with a unique fourth Discipline or be locked only to a single clan?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. I merely refuted that we had reason to believe that the design philosophy for Bloodlines would steer away from unique Disciplines when those were the only non-experimental examples we had prior to Spilled Blood.<br /> <br /> It's not that I don't like the wildly different places a Bloodline can take you. What I dislike is how Bloodlines represents a wide swath of concepts that all have to fight for the same space on the character sheet. Embraced to a particular dynasty? Well now you can never join this Covenant subgroup, or suffer from this horrible curse, or make a deal with this demon, or develop a Bloodline of your own, etc.<br /> I'm also not a fan of most Bloodlines being Clan exclusive. I guess it's thematic, but I don't think it being thematic makes up for how restrictive it is for both players and ST. (I hear that Spilled Blood has opened up that a bit, but back in 1e it was so bad that even the Moroi had a text explaining that it was actually just two identical Bloodlines; one for Gangrels and one for Nosteratu.)<br /> <br /> What I would've preferred is a division of &quot;dynastic&quot; Bloodlines and &quot;social&quot; Bloodlines, as well as other &quot;quirks of the Blood&quot;. Let Kindred dynasties have their own little quirks (like a fourth non-unique Discipline or affinity with certain Skills) that reinforces the themes of blood ties. Open up Covenant subgroups (or other social/ideological Bloodlines) for membership from all Clans by leveraging access to their advantages (whether they be uncommon Disciplines, Devotions or even Merits) with responsibilities and social bonds. And let the really weird shit stay weird and not force it into the same old Bloodline model as everything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T15:05:36-08:00","id":1367885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367413-what-makes-a-bloodline-a-bloodline?p=1367873#post1367873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems an odd position to take. They're as official as anything else. Especially given they are listed in the <i>Official </i>Resources post by Rose and posted on the official website/blog.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are <i>explicitly</i> experimental and unpolished, and they do date before Rose Bailey left as the VtR lead dev. They might've been indicative of the design philosophy back then, but we don't have the same person at the helm of VtR anymore and the only two recent examples prior to Spilled Blood used a unique fourth Discipline. If anyone were to base their theory about current Bloodline design philosophy (despite the very low amount of examples available) it would make a lot more sense to base it on the most recent examples that also were the only ones that made it into books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T18:38:34-08:00","id":1367947,"title":"","content":"The bloodlines in Spilled Blood almost exactly follow Rose's guide. That can't be a coincidence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In first edition, bloodlines were meant to be a make-your-own- clan system. But we were somewhat confused on whether they were \u201cprestige classes\u201d you advanced into, societies you joined, or things you inherited.<br /> They should have the potential to be all three. But that means that adding a five-dot Discipline for every one doesn\u2019t make sense.<br /> <br /> Take, for example, the Macellarius. This gruesome and very fun Ventrue (or are they Julii?) bloodline is distinguished by eating flesh. This isn\u2019t a trick you should have to buy dot by dot, it should be a big jump in how your vampirism works.<br /> Or the Galloi, blood-bathers whose strange beauty should really be a base power and then twists on Majesty.<br /> The luck-manipulation of the Bogahande fits into a Discipline ladder, but why does someone cursed/blessed with it have to buy in? The solution is simply to not have all bloodlines work the same. But there are still best practices.<br /> <br /> Most bloodlines should have one to two of the following:<br /> \u2022 Modifications to their core vampiric abilities<br /> \u2022 Special Devotions<br /> \u2022 A new Discipline<br /> \u2022 Merits relating to the social benefits/effects of bloodline membership</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}